Tremulous Revamped (Windows x64 and Linux x86_64)
=================================================

Play: unzip anywhere, then
  Windows: run Tremulous.exe
  Linux:   run ./Tremulous.x86_64   (if it does not start: chmod +x Tremulous.x86_64)
Both share one base/ folder and the same Tremulous.pck.

Linux requirements: 64-bit Linux with glibc @REQ@ or newer, a Vulkan 1.1 or
OpenGL 3.3 driver, X11 or Wayland. Sound on Linux uses Godot's own audio (the FMOD
and Steam Audio files fmod.dll, phonon*.dll, trem_audio.dll are Windows-only).

4K textures (optional): download both tremulous-revamped-hd-textures zips from
the Tremulous-Revamped GitHub release "hd-textures-v1" and unzip them into this
folder, so you get an "hd" folder next to the executable (used by both systems).

base/ holds the original Tremulous 1.1 content (see base/COPYING, base/CC and
base/README.txt).
Source code: https://github.com/MeepingsCorner/Tremulous-Revamped (this port);
the original Tremulous code it is ported from: https://github.com/darklegion/tremulous-legacy
